Notebook[
 {Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Tree-level graviton scattering with FeynArts", 
      "Title", ExpressionUUID -> "14a74f86-b215-4b20-94e3-aff4e139f2e7"], 
     Cell["Generate and display all four off-shell 2 -> 2 graviton tree \
diagrams with FeynArts: the three exchange channels and the quartic contact. \
Attach unconstrained external polarisation tensors, contract each \
contribution, and store their sum in \[ScriptCapitalM]. No mass-shell, \
transversality, tracelessness or helicity conditions are imposed.", "Text", 
      ExpressionUUID -> "dc7be9f0-e01f-482e-b16b-a401a43db518"], 
     Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["1. Initialisation", "Section", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "66979d8e-122c-4326-a3d4-6b1c333b6c2c"], 
        Cell["Start with a fresh kernel (especially after running the \
previous on-shell version) and evaluate the two cells below with Shift+Enter. \
The first loads FeynGrav, which loads FeynCalc and CalcFormConverter, and \
asks FeynCalc to load the installed patched FeynArts. The saved pure-GR model \
uses gauge parameter 2 and contains the cubic and quartic graviton \
interactions and gravitational ghosts. GenericModel is given explicitly \
because the classes file does not name its generic model and the FeynArts \
default is the stock \"Lorentz\" file. No diagrams are generated and FORM is \
not executed here. Opening this notebook executes nothing.", "Text", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "3f444fd2-0054-4d3a-9b81-971cc7884bc8"], 
        Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell[BoxData[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"$LoadAddOns", "=", 
                  RowBox[{"{", "\"FeynArts\"", "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
